WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.501
Tonight as we continue to

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.703
report the fallout from Donald Trump's

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.338
criminal indictment.

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:06.039
We're talking to

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:08.208
perhaps the most famous Republican

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:10.877
in the country outside of Trump himself

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:12.846
about the federal case

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:14.581
against the former president.

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:15.482
The current state

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:17.851
of our deeply divided country

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:19.052
and the one frame,

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:21.221
even this bodybuilder turned movie

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:23.323
star turned politician

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:25.658
could not make come true.

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:28.194
Former California Governor Arnold

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.996
Schwarzenegger

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:31.765
Arnold Schwarzenegger, welcome.

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:33.166
It's great to talk to you again.

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:35.101
And I want to start with the basics.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.537
Do you prefer being called governor

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:39.406
or Arnold

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.808
It makes no difference to me.

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:44.010
I get called anything and everything.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:44.544
You know,

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:45.678
when I go to Sacramento,

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:47.113
they call me the governor

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:48.415
and they go down to the Gold's Gym

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:49.516
they call me Arnold

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:50.417
and they go to Austria.

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:51.851
The call me schnitzel

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:52.852
or Kraut or whatever.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:54.788
I mean, so I get every title

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:55.655
that you could think of.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:56.155
Well,

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.158
to close between Arnold and schnitzel,

00:00:58.158 --> 00:00:59.426
but I think I'll go with Arnold

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:00.293
Schwarzenegger.

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:01.661
The Constitution said

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:02.629
that a president

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:06.132
has to be a natural born U.S.

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:08.501
citizen, if not for that.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.538
Would you have run for president?

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:13.907
Well, yes, of course.

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:14.574
I mean,

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:17.177
I think the field was wide open in 2016

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:20.547
and I think the field is open right now.

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:21.981
I mean, think about it right now.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:25.652
I mean, who is there

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:26.553
that is

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:28.021
really a person

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:30.123
that can bring everyone together.

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.091
Who is the other day

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:33.426
that people say, okay, he's not too old

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:35.295
or he's not to this to do that?

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:36.029
Or is that

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:37.630
because it's now a question about

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.099
who do you vote against

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:40.433
rather than who do you vote for?

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:41.568
So you're saying you would run

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:44.037
for president in 20, 24? Absolutely.

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:46.973
Because it's a look it's a no brainer

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.876
I see so clearly how he could win

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:51.778
the election.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:55.248
I mean, it's like me in California in it

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.082
when I was,

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:57.884
you know, running for governor,

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.252
it was clear

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.153
that people are looking

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:01.921
for some new answer,

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.690
not a right wing or a left wing,

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:04.457
but someone that can

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.126
bring the nation together.

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:07.794
This is just so many things

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.796
that need to be done and can be done.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.064
And what makes it so wonderful

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:12.499
is because it's doable.

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:13.366
It's all doable.

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:14.200
All it needs is just

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.668
people coming together

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:17.737
and saying, yes, we can do it.

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:20.840
You've put out some videos

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.008
in recent years

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:24.077
that I want to ask you about.

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:25.411
You put out

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:26.212
this video

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:28.448
right after the insurrection

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:30.283
on January 6th. Take a look

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:33.920
Wednesday was the day of

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.054
broken glass right here

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:36.956
in the United States.

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:38.791
The broken glass was in the windows

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.493
of the United States Capitol.

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:43.062
President Trump is a failed leader.

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:44.264
He will go down in history

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:47.100
as the worst president ever.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:47.767
The good thing is

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:48.434
the decision

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.870
will be as irrelevant as an old tweet.

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:54.674
Another night of broken glass or crystal

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:58.178
knock was in 1938 when Nazi sympathizers

00:02:58.178 --> 00:03:01.681
ransacked Jewish stores and

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:05.018
and synagogues and schools.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:08.154
Do you still think it's fair to compare

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:11.691
Kristallnacht, the Nazi

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:12.859
attack on the Jews,

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:14.761
to what happened on January 6th?

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:15.895
Yeah, absolutely.

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:17.197
I mean, I think that is

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:19.866
of course a different time and all that.

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:21.134
But it is kind of like

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:24.571
a threat to democracy and a threat

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:26.172
of what happens to people

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:27.840
when they're lied to.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.442
And this is why I compared it to that

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:31.477
because in Kristallnacht and to the

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:32.845
I know with my father

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:35.548
who was part of the Nazi Party,

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.050
you know, they were lied to,

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.451
they were misled.

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:40.253
And I think a lot of people in America

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:41.921
today are being misled.

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:44.757
But you were wrong about Donald Trump.

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:47.327
You said he's going to be irrelevant.

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:48.795
He's not.

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:49.562
In fact, he's

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.231
the leading candidate

00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:52.966
for the Republican nomination.

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:55.535
It's you know, we don't know the future.

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:57.337
I just predicted that.

00:03:57.337 --> 00:03:58.271
But we will see.

00:03:58.271 --> 00:04:00.473
And remember, the future still goes on

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:02.675
So we will see in the few years from now

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:03.543
how right it was

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:05.311
and that I cannot prove it right now.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.413
But eventually I think it will be true.

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:08.414
I will be right

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.084
now Mr.

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:12.252
Trump has been

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:14.520
indicted on federal charges,

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:18.258
but most of the top Republican officials

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:19.726
are siding with him

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:21.828
against the special prosecutor.

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:25.064
How do you explain that?

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:26.699
Well, first of all,

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:29.335
I'm not an expert in this issue.

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:31.471
I just can tell you one thing, that

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:34.307
if the charges are correct,

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:37.543
then he's going to be in deep trouble.

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:40.980
But at the same time, I have to say that,

00:04:41.681 --> 00:04:42.015
you know,

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:43.983
we always innocent until proven guilty.

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:46.019
So we will find out what the courts say

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:47.020
in the future.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.721
But, I mean, if the judges are right,

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:49.055
I think

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:50.857
there's going to be in deep trouble.

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:52.292
And how worried are you about

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:53.192
the fact that

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:56.129
he could be reelected president?

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:58.298
I'm not worried about it

00:04:58.298 --> 00:04:58.998
because I don't think

00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:00.433
it's going to happen.

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:02.201
I just don't think that you get reelected

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:03.069
with 30%

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:04.771
or 33% of the people

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:05.405
voting for you

00:05:05.405 --> 00:05:07.940
all you need in your polls.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.242
I think that's dead.

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:10.410
There's a great poll numbers

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.045
among conservatives,

00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:14.380
but I think if you put it all together,

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:15.181
it's not enough.

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:16.182
You need to swing voters.

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:17.150
You need independents.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:19.252
And so the question is, can you do that?

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:21.454
I, I believe he can.

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:24.757
In March, you put out another video

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:26.793
about the rise of anti-Semitism

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:28.961
in this country and around the world.

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:29.595
Here you are

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:34.067
there
has never been a successful movement

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:35.268
based on hate.

00:05:35.268 --> 00:05:36.736
I mean, think about that.

00:05:36.736 --> 00:05:38.938
The Nazis losers,

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:41.307
the Confederacy

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:43.910
loses, the apartheid movement loses,

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:47.146
and the list goes on and on.

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:50.850
I don't want you to be a loser.

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:54.354
How do you explain all the hate

00:05:54.354 --> 00:05:56.789
and what do you think it will take

00:05:56.789 --> 00:05:57.857
in the U.S.

00:05:57.857 --> 00:05:59.892
and around the world for the fever,

00:05:59.892 --> 00:06:02.462
the hate to end?

00:06:02.462 --> 00:06:03.930
I mean, people really are starving

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:05.231
for something positive.

00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:08.468
There's just so much on social media

00:06:08.468 --> 00:06:10.570
and online out there that is negative

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:12.038
negative, negative, negative.

00:06:12.038 --> 00:06:13.172
So, you know,

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:15.575
I think that has an impact on people

00:06:15.575 --> 00:06:16.909
the way they feel about things.

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:18.244
And so what I want to do is

00:06:18.244 --> 00:06:18.811
I want to

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:21.114
pull people out of that negativism

00:06:21.414 --> 00:06:22.749
and just make them

00:06:22.749 --> 00:06:24.817
give them something positive

00:06:24.817 --> 00:06:26.686
to tell them that they're good.

00:06:26.686 --> 00:06:28.087
Tell them their training well.

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:29.722
Tell them that they're in good shape,

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:30.790
that there is hope for them

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:31.691
in all of this stuff.

00:06:31.691 --> 00:06:33.326
And so I just

00:06:33.326 --> 00:06:34.260
I think this is where

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:35.762
the action is today.

00:06:35.762 --> 00:06:37.597
And I'm always been an optimist.

00:06:37.597 --> 00:06:39.665
I always have been the positive person

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:40.700
and yes,

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:41.401
there's a lot of things

00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:42.001
I don't like,

00:06:42.001 --> 00:06:42.702
but it doesn't mean that

00:06:42.702 --> 00:06:44.637
I have to hate the people.

00:06:44.637 --> 00:06:45.571
And I think that's what we

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:46.773
have to do about racial

00:06:48.875 --> 00:06:49.442
problems.

00:06:49.442 --> 00:06:51.978
That we have about, you know,

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:56.182
gay people and all of this kind of stuff.

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:59.652
Immigrants and Mexicans and Russians

00:06:59.652 --> 00:07:00.186
and this,

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:01.220
we just have to go

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:02.755
and just come together.

00:07:02.755 --> 00:07:03.923
It doesn't matter who it is,

00:07:03.923 --> 00:07:05.425
no matter how different they are

00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:07.860
and respect them as human beings

00:07:08.261 --> 00:07:10.363
and try to see their point of view.

00:07:11.564 --> 00:07:13.533
You're also deeply involved

00:07:13.533 --> 00:07:14.434
in the environment.

00:07:14.434 --> 00:07:15.835
You run
an annual conference

00:07:15.835 --> 00:07:18.271
called the Austrian World Summit.

00:07:18.471 --> 00:07:19.172
You said something

00:07:19.172 --> 00:07:21.374
interesting recently that

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:26.012
you don't like the phrase climate change.

00:07:26.145 --> 00:07:27.413
You think it's bad marketing.

00:07:27.413 --> 00:07:28.481
What do you mean?

00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:29.282
Well,

00:07:29.549 --> 00:07:32.151
because when you talk about climate

00:07:32.151 --> 00:07:32.552
change, it's

00:07:32.552 --> 00:07:33.653
something that always is

00:07:33.653 --> 00:07:34.720
referred to as something

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.189
that is going to happen

00:07:36.189 --> 00:07:37.190
down the line

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:39.091
or it's going to gradually happen

00:07:39.091 --> 00:07:40.293
and people's minds.

00:07:41.294 --> 00:07:41.961
Our brain

00:07:41.961 --> 00:07:44.063
is not wired to respond

00:07:44.063 --> 00:07:45.465
to something down the line.

00:07:45.465 --> 00:07:46.399
So therefore,

00:07:46.399 --> 00:07:46.732
let's

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:47.633
look at something

00:07:47.633 --> 00:07:48.501
that is really

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:50.203
the cause of climate change,

00:07:50.203 --> 00:07:51.471
which is pollution.

00:07:51.471 --> 00:07:54.540
If we fight pollution,

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:57.510
then everyone will get on board.

00:07:57.510 --> 00:07:59.545
But if you say climate change,

00:07:59.545 --> 00:08:00.613
the Republicans

00:08:00.613 --> 00:08:02.915
will immediately run the other way

00:08:02.915 --> 00:08:04.717
because it's one of those buzzwords

00:08:04.717 --> 00:08:05.952
that they hate.

00:08:05.952 --> 00:08:06.686
According to the World

00:08:06.686 --> 00:08:08.521
Health Organization, 7 million people

00:08:08.521 --> 00:08:09.355
a year die

00:08:09.355 --> 00:08:10.790
because of pollution,

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:12.525
not because of climate change.

00:08:12.525 --> 00:08:13.659
Yes, there's maybe

00:08:13.659 --> 00:08:15.194
a few hundred people dying here and there

00:08:15.194 --> 00:08:16.562
because of a flood of fire

00:08:16.562 --> 00:08:17.630
or something like that.

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:19.866
But not like pollution.

00:08:19.866 --> 00:08:22.101
So we should talk about pollution.

00:08:22.101 --> 00:08:23.736
That is what works.

00:08:23.736 --> 00:08:26.239
You are so busy these days.

00:08:26.239 --> 00:08:29.041
You are starring in a wildly popular

00:08:29.275 --> 00:08:30.776
series on Netflix,

00:08:30.776 --> 00:08:33.012
your first TV series called FUBAR,

00:08:33.412 --> 00:08:36.983
in which you play a CIA operative

00:08:36.983 --> 00:08:38.518
who's just about to retire

00:08:38.518 --> 00:08:40.119
when he's called out

00:08:40.119 --> 00:08:40.520
to help

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:42.588
save another operative who turns out

00:08:43.222 --> 00:08:45.157
to be his daughter. Here you are.

00:08:46.325 --> 00:08:47.660
I'm a I'm a parent.

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:48.961
Take him out

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:52.465
Bouncing all over the place

00:08:52.465 --> 00:08:53.432
and get a shot off.

00:08:53.432 --> 00:08:55.968
You were able to hit me

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:18.858
that was my lead from

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:22.995
I got to say, the story's fine,

00:09:22.995 --> 00:09:24.230
but for me,

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:26.032
the delight is seeing Arnold

00:09:26.032 --> 00:09:27.733
be Arnold again.

00:09:27.733 --> 00:09:31.270
But well, I think that it's one of those

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:35.341
kind of great TV series

00:09:36.108 --> 00:09:38.377
that was so well-written

00:09:38.377 --> 00:09:40.413
that I could be myself

00:09:40.413 --> 00:09:42.014
I could do the humor,

00:09:42.014 --> 00:09:43.182
I could do the action,

00:09:43.182 --> 00:09:44.850
I could do the serious stuff.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:45.184
I mean,

00:09:45.184 --> 00:09:46.986
it gives with all the different layers.

00:09:46.986 --> 00:09:48.321
So it was just well-written.

00:09:48.321 --> 00:09:49.922
The writers were fantastic.

00:09:49.922 --> 00:09:51.123
And they did a really great job.

00:09:51.123 --> 00:09:51.958
And they promised me

00:09:51.958 --> 00:09:53.626
they're going to go and deliver to me

00:09:53.626 --> 00:09:54.393
eight scripts

00:09:54.393 --> 00:09:55.328
that are very close

00:09:55.328 --> 00:09:57.496
to the idea of True Lies.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:59.632
Then I believe them,

00:09:59.632 --> 00:10:01.567
and they pulled it off.

00:10:01.567 --> 00:10:04.170
Okay, you're 75 years old.

00:10:04.403 --> 00:10:06.405
You've got all the money in the world.

00:10:06.572 --> 00:10:07.740
Why on earth

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:10.076
are you jumping around moving vehicles?

00:10:11.744 --> 00:10:13.412
Well, to be honest with you, Chris,

00:10:13.412 --> 00:10:16.248
I don't think I ever was motivated

00:10:16.248 --> 00:10:17.783
by anything that I've done

00:10:17.783 --> 00:10:19.018
because of money.

00:10:19.018 --> 00:10:21.420
It was always just because I enjoyed.

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:23.022
I love bodybuilding

00:10:23.022 --> 00:10:24.557
and loves getting into movies

00:10:24.557 --> 00:10:25.891
and doing all the scenes.

00:10:25.891 --> 00:10:26.258
Yes.

00:10:26.258 --> 00:10:28.260
You you go and start

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:29.428
getting more and more money

00:10:29.428 --> 00:10:30.830
because that's your value.

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:32.331
But it's not about that.

00:10:32.331 --> 00:10:33.265
You really have to love

00:10:33.265 --> 00:10:33.899
what you're doing.

00:10:33.899 --> 00:10:35.401
So why are you doing that?

00:10:35.401 --> 00:10:36.435
I just love doing it.

00:10:36.435 --> 00:10:37.536
It's always every day,

00:10:37.536 --> 00:10:39.071
something different and I love that.

